# =============================================================================
# greeter/qmldir — the login screen's one piece of shared state
# =============================================================================
# GreeterState is a SINGLETON: there is exactly one of it, and anything in the
# login screen can reach it without being handed a reference.
#
# It has to be a singleton rather than an object somebody owns, because the
# login screen draws one full-screen window PER MONITOR, and all of those
# windows are looking at the same one question — who is logging in, with which
# password, into which desktop. Two copies of that state on a two-monitor
# machine would be a bug you only find when you plug a second screen in.
#
# QML will not treat a file as a singleton on the strength of its `pragma
# Singleton` line alone — it also has to be named here. Forget this and the
# login screen fails to start with "GreeterState is not a type", which is a
# confusing way to be told you did not write it down.
# =============================================================================

singleton GreeterState 1.0 GreeterState.qml
